  "summary_en": "African Union continental AI strategy adopted July 2024. It sets an Africa-centric, development-oriented approach with five focus areas and fifteen policy actions covering AI governance, public sector and sector adoption, capacity, infrastructure, investment, risk mitigation and cooperation. It has no robotics-specific provisions.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Five focus areas: harness benefits, build capabilities, minimise risks, stimulate investment, foster cooperation",
   "Fifteen action areas, starting with AI governance systems and regulation at regional and national levels",
   "Calls for AI infrastructure, data, skills and research investment across member states",
   "Addresses bias, disinformation, privacy, job displacement and human rights risks, including from generative AI",
   "Urges member states to domesticate the strategy into national AI policies"
